From cf9551560461f092bd47d19ca1ad9787aea738ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Drabik <drabikp@posam.sk>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:54:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Device hooks for panels with a physically covered bottom
 corner

Two dimensions, both 0dp by default, for a cover display whose bottom corner is
occluded by a rear camera block (Motorola razr 50 ultra: 495x349 px at the
bottom right of a 1080x1272 panel):

- hotseat_bar_bottom_space_extra: added to hotseatBarBottomSpacePx so the dock
  can sit above the covered area.
- taskbar_ime_bottom_inset_override: the taskbar's navigationBars provider gets
  an InsetsSizeOverride for TYPE_INPUT_METHOD (portrait only), so the keyboard
  positions itself above the covered area while apps and the launcher keep the
  real bar height. Same mechanism the taskbar already uses for the assistant
  window.

Declaring the block as a display cutout is not an option on AOSP: a bottom-edge
cutout becomes a full-width safe inset and every edge-to-edge app ends its
scroll views above it, so 27% of the panel cannot start a scroll.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
